/// DOM backend for the `text` device — merged under `[select] text = "dom"`. The web-overlay renderer: each
/// display run becomes one absolutely-positioned <span> over the gfx <canvas> (real browser fonts). Like
/// gfx/wasm there is NO C shim: `text_be_*` stay undefined and become wasm IMPORTS the JS host (www/text.js)
/// fulfils by creating/positioning <span>s. The seams are `#module`-private. Not a standalone test.
///
/// `render` re-emits every run each frame (clear + draw = an idempotent redraw), so world signs whose `tx,ty`
/// the driver reprojects per frame track the scrolling scene. It reads the same driver display-run columns the
/// framebuffer backend does, so a driver's text code is identical across backends. `tstr` (a `[N]char` buffer)
/// crosses as a bare pointer; `tlen` is the live length.
#module
#foreign
text_be_draw  :: proc(x: int, y: int, own s: []char, n: int, size: int, color: int);
text_be_clear :: proc();

/// Clear last frame's spans, then emit one <span> per display run at its projected (tx,ty).
render :: system eff {
  text_be_clear()();
  map (query { tx, ty, tstr, tlen, tsz, tcol }) eff {
    text_be_draw(tx, ty, tstr, tlen, tsz, tcol)();
  };
}
